#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:2
msgid "Poetry plugin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:4
msgid ""
"The poethepoet poetry plugin offers tighter integration with the poetry CLI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:7
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:9
msgid "You can install the poethepoet poetry plugin globally like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:11
msgid "poetry self add 'poethepoet[poetry_plugin]'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:15
msgid ""
"Or add it to poetry on a per project basis by adding the following to your "
"*pyproject.toml*:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:17
msgid ""
"[tool.poetry.requires-plugins]\n"
"poethepoet = { version = \"~0.35.0\", extras = [\"poetry_plugin\"]}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:22
msgid ""
"See the |poetry_plugin_link| for more installation options, or see the :doc:"
"`poetry plugin docs <poetry_plugin>` for more details about this option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:139
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://python-poetry.org/docs/plugins/#using-plugins\" "
"target=\"_blank\">poetry plugin</a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:26
msgid "Configuring the plugin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:28
msgid ""
"By default the poetry plugin will register *poe* as a command prefix so "
"tasks can be invoked like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:31
msgid "poetry poe [task_name] [task_args]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:35
msgid "And the poe documentation can be viewed via:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:37
msgid "poetry poe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:41
msgid ""
"It is also possible to modify this behavior, to either have a different "
"command prefix or none at all by setting the :toml:`poetry_command` global "
"option in your pyproject.toml like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:45
msgid ""
"[tool.poe]\n"
"poetry_command = \"\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:50
msgid ""
"In this case poe tasks will be registered as top level commands on poetry "
"and can be invoked simply as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:53
msgid "poetry [task_name]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:58
msgid ""
"Whatever :toml:`tool.poe.poetry_command` is set to must not already exist as "
"a poetry command!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:61
msgid ""
"Additionally if setting it to the empty string then care must be taken to "
"avoid defining any poe tasks that conflict with any other built in or plugin "
"provided poetry command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:66
msgid "Hooking into poetry commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:68
msgid ""
"It is also possible to configure a task to be run before or after a specific "
"poetry command by declaring the ``poetry_hooks`` global option like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:71
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.poetry_hooks]\n"
"pre_build  = \"prep-assets --verbosity=5\"\n"
"post_build = \"archive-build\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.prep-assets]\n"
"script = \"scripts:prepare_assets\"\n"
"help   = \"Optimise static assets for inclusion in the build\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.poe.tasks.archive-build]\n"
"script = \"scripts:archive_build\"\n"
"help   = \"Upload the latest build version to the archive server\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:85
msgid ""
"In this example the ``prep-assets`` task will be run as the first step when "
"calling :sh:`poetry build` with an argument passed as if the task were being "
"called via the poe CLI. We've also configured the ``archive-build`` task to "
"be run after every successful build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:90
msgid ""
"If a task fails when running as a hook, then the poetry command will exit "
"with an error. If it is a *pre* hook then this will cause the actual poetry "
"command not to execute. This behaviour may be useful for running checks "
"before :bash:`poetry publish`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:94
msgid ""
"Hooks can be disabled for a single invocation by passing the :bash:`--no-"
"plugins` option to poetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:97
msgid ""
"Namespaced commands like :bash:`poetry env info` can be specified with "
"underscores like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:99
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.poetry_hooks]\n"
"post_env_info = \"info\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:104
msgid "All poetry commands are supported in principle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:107
msgid "Known limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:109
msgid ""
"Due to how the poetry CLI works (using |cleo_link| — a featureful but highly "
"opinionated CLI framework) there exist a few minor limitations to consider "
"when using the Poe the Poet poetry plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:131
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://github.com/python-poetry/cleo\" target=\"_blank\">cleo</a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:114
msgid ""
"Normally the poe CLI allows tasks to accept any arguments, either by "
"defining the expected options or by passing any command line tokens "
"following the task name to the task at runtime. This is not supported by "
"cleo. The plugin implements a workaround that mostly works, but still if the "
"`--no-plugins` option is provided *anywhere* in the command line then the "
"poe plugin will never be invoked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:121
msgid ""
"Poetry comes with its own |poetry_comp_link|, which includes completion of "
"task names but poe's command line completion won't work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:135
msgid ""
"<a href=\"https://python-poetry.org/docs/#enable-tab-completion-for-bash-"
"fish-or-zsh\" target=\"_blank\">command line completion</a>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:124
msgid ""
"If you declare named arguments for your poe tasks then these are included in "
"the documentation when poe is invoked without any arguments. However the "
"inline documentation for poetry commands contains only the task names and "
"help text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../poetry_plugin.rst:128
msgid ""
"Therefore it is generally recommended to use the poe CLI tool directly if "
"you don't mind having it installed onto your path."
msgstr ""
